              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Portuguese for the written report, then the Portuguese for to announce in the news."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: a declaração",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a declaração — \"the declaration, the public statement\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "O presidente fez uma declaração aos jornalistas. The president made a statement to the journalists."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fazer uma declaração — to make a statement. Also a form you fill in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "declaração is a learned borrowing from Latin dēclārātiō \"a making clear\" (EtymDB), from dēclārāre, built on clārus \"clear\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
